      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rematch news",
          "heading": "Fiji's 21-16 victims Italy lose Miotti and Ferrari for Twickenham rematch",
          "body": "Fiji meet Italy again at Twickenham in a match that settles 11th and 12th place in the Nations Championship, and the Azzurri must reshuffle at fly-half. Domingo Miotti, who left the field in the 48th minute in Udine, has a left hamstring injury and returns to Montpellier for rehabilitation. Prop Simone Ferrari withdrew an hour before kick-off with a left upper-limb injury and goes back to Treviso. Italy do welcome back Lynagh. Centre Leonardo Marin admitted his side conceded too many stupid penalties in the second half."
        },
