      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rotation vow",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy vows Wales rotation for Japan play-off after 26-29 Australia loss",
          "body": "Tandy doubled down after the game on Saturday night: \"I can rotate the team and we'll still put in a performance. It doesn't matter who wears the shirt, we've got to perform.\" Eleven players started against Japan, New Zealand and Australia, so this weekend's 9th/10th play-off against the Brave Blossoms at Twickenham's Allianz Stadium offers a rare look at depth. Alex Cuthbert wants the frontline kept on; Japan, stretched by injury, conceded 24 tries losing to England and Scotland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 to set up Australia finals clash",
