    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Costly night",
          "heading": "Delguy and Wenger forced off as Vivas red card sinks Pumas 45-17",
          "body": "Argentina's 45-17 loss to France at the Stade de France came at a cost. Bautista Delguy and Boris Wenger went off early and did not return, after Santiago Chocobares had withdrawn hours before kick-off, with Justo Piccardo starting at inside centre. The Pumas led 10-7 before trailing 14-10 at the break. Hollie Davidson's yellow for Mayco Vivas was upgraded to red, Julián Montoya was then sin-binned, and France cashed in with three tries. Scotland await in the battle for seventh."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 to set up Australia finals clash",
          "body": "France recall Thomas Ramos for Springboks final. South Africa's Marco van Staden likely banned for France final."
