    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ikitau revived",
          "heading": "Len Ikitau backs Wallabies defence after man-of-the-match display in 29-26 win",
          "body": "A try, an assist and a match-high 15 carries in Cardiff capped a stop-start year for the 2025 John Eales Medal winner. Shoulder surgery, an ankle injury against South Africa and a concussion that wrecked his Bledisloe Cup hopes all interrupted it. Ikitau credited the system under new defence coach Scott McLeod: \"defensively, we've taken a step up.\" Ireland, Friday's fifth-place play-off opponents at Twickenham, may be without Dan Sheehan, whose yellow card against South Africa was upgraded to red."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina lose 45-17 to France after Mayco Vivas red card",
          "body": "France recall Thomas Ramos for Springboks final. South Africa's Marco van Staden likely banned for France final."
