    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Jones on Townsend",
          "heading": "Japan's Eddie Jones hailed Townsend's Scotland two days before 67-5 rout",
          "body": "Japan's coach had talked up the opposition before last Saturday's Nations Championship meeting, and Scotland then put 11 tries past his side in a 67-5 win at Murrayfield. Speaking on the Thursday, Jones said: “Gregor’s done a great job, and I think Scotland should be grateful for the job that he’s done.” He argued Scotland were performing well for a country with two professional teams to pick from. Takuro Matsunaga scored Japan's only try — in the second half — after the hosts led 29-0 at the break."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat Springboks 20-17 to set up Australia finals clash",
          "body": "Argentina lose 45-17 to France after Mayco Vivas red card. France recall Thomas Ramos for Springboks final. South Africa's Marco van Staden likely banned for France final."
