    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Wilson's verdict",
          "heading": "Jeff Wilson says All Blacks 'had no energy' in 37-12 England loss",
          "body": "Former wing Jeff Wilson, speaking on The Breakdown, said the side looked physically and emotionally drained at Twickenham and \"just looked as though they were done.\" The defeat was New Zealand's fifth Test loss of the season, the most since 1998, and came a week after their first defeat to Wales since 1953. Wilson missed Ruben Love's combination with Damian McKenzie but argued there was enough talent on the field, and that some reputations had been dented. England await in the third-place playoff."
        },
        {
